# Memory session-continuity MINOR

TBD-AT-SEAL. Sealed local; awaiting dispatcher dogfood publish per ASK-FIRST.

A session restart is behaviourally transparent. File-based memory
makes sessions not matter: a fresh session reconstructs the active
working thread + live decisions / pending rulings from durably-stored
memory read at session-start, without any bespoke session-end capture
hook. Continuous passive capture already exists and is healthy; the
fix is read-side + ranking-side only.

Closes Gap B (recency never a ranking signal — file_memory.py:489
ORDER BY pure BM25, reference_time UNINDEXED) via recency-aware
ranking, and Gap A (named-thread durable surfaces absent from the
session-start corpus + episode memory never read at session-start)
via a new TriggerKind.session active-thread contributor composed on
the SEALED #45/#46 SessionStart substrate plus named-thread surfaces
entering the session-start corpus as defence-in-depth.

Composes with: #32/#33 D8/D7 composer + memory-consumer; the M-FBM
file-based pivot (graphiti out of the runtime path); v0.4.3 BM25-fix
(token sanitisation already sealed — out of scope here); #45
multi-contributor SessionStart registry; #46 session-start emitter.
